BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20251006T130000Z
DTEND:20251006T140000Z
SUMMARY:Internship Applications Open
DESCRIPTION:The goal of the Office of Sustainability &amp\; Campus Enrich
 ment's Internship Program is to bring undergraduate students from a varie
 ty of backgrounds and perspectives together to create a dynamic team that
  works to create a culture of sustainability at Texas A&amp\;M University
 . Interns work together to increase awareness and education about the thr
 ee pillars of sustainability: environmental\, economic\, and social. The 
 team focuses on educating the campus community about topics such as: ener
 gy and water use\, transportation\, food services\, construction and buil
 t environment\, purchasing\, recycling\, and social sustainability throug
 h the development of outreach initiatives and event coordination. Additio
 nally\, interns support assessment and planning efforts prioritized by th
 e office.  The Internship Program is open to any TAMU undergraduate stude
 nt and all majors are encouraged to apply because true sustainability mus
 t be an interdisciplinary enterprise.  Applications are open October 6\, 
 2025 – November 9\, 2025 at sustainability.tamu.edu.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The goal of the Office of Sustainabilit
 y &amp\; Campus Enrichment's Internship Program is to bring undergraduate
  students from a variety of backgrounds and perspectives together to crea
 te a dynamic team that works to create a culture of sustainability at Tex
 as A&amp\;M University. Interns work together to increase awareness and e
 ducation about the three pillars of sustainability: environmental\, econo
 mic\, and social. The team focuses on educating the campus community abou
 t topics such as: energy and water use\, transportation\, food services\,
  construction and built environment\, purchasing\, recycling\, and social
  sustainability through the development of outreach initiatives and event
  coordination. Additionally\, interns support assessment and planning eff
 orts prioritized by the office.<br /><br />  The Internship Program is op
 en to any TAMU undergraduate student and all majors are encouraged to app
 ly because true sustainability must be an interdisciplinary enterprise.<b
 r /><br />  Applications are open October 6\, 2025 – November 9\, 2025 
 at sustainability.tamu.edu.</p>
